{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only","id":1358884,"title":"What do you love about Exalted? [Positive Responses Only]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-04T08:53:57-08:00","id":1358884,"title":"What do you love about Exalted? [Positive Responses Only]","content":"As one of the freelance writers these days, I don't get too directly involved with the fan community, but Exalted has given me a lot of enjoyment and inspiration. I've seen &quot;positive responses only&quot; threads on other forums, and I think it'd be an interesting experiment for this one. Please join me in this experiment. I doubt we'll do it perfectly, but a good-faith effort would be appreciated. If it's been done already, well, the search function didn't reveal that to me, and also, who cares.<br /> <br /> For me: I still love writing Charms (and I hope people enjoy what I recently wrote for <i>Exigents</i>). I love the mythic weight of the Exalted. As someone who started with D&amp;D, I loved Exalted's willingness to address sex and sexuality, and love that we've been moving toward healthier ways to discuss those topics in the current edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T09:36:02-08:00","id":1358890,"title":"","content":"The incredibly broad range of potential characters. A starting circle can happily include a merchant prince, a destitute waif, a famous poet and a grizzled warlord without any problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T09:44:40-08:00","id":1358892,"title":"","content":"1) It's not eurofantasy.<br /> 2) You can have a concept like bureaucrat, blacksmith, socialite, preacher, sailor, etc, and the game actually supports making it a major part of your character, rather than an add-on to your combat focus.<br /> 3) Pulp sorcery<br /> 4) Big, dramatic stories that reshape countries or even the world<br /> 5) I quite enjoy the base combat system (in 3rd ed)<br /> 6) The authors actually thought through the societies they created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T09:51:24-08:00","id":1358893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1358890#post1358890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The incredibly broad range of potential characters. A starting circle can happily include a merchant prince, a destitute waif, a famous poet and a grizzled warlord without any problems.</div> </div> </div> </div> I enjoy the flexibility but also the challenge of running for such a group and trying to keep everyone engaged.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T10:00:23-08:00","id":1358894,"title":"","content":"I love that homebrew is given a prominent place in the game.<br /> <br /> I love that you're <u>allowed</u> to break the game.<br /> <br /> I love that the game lets you try crazy plans or ideas which would be far too punishing to try in a different game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T10:37:51-08:00","id":1358899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1358894#post1358894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love that the game lets you try crazy plans or ideas which would be far too punishing to try in a different game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a challlenge to run for this but it's also so satisfying when a player knocks down all my careful dominoes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T11:30:05-08:00","id":1358906,"title":"","content":"I like how the setting was built to readily accommodate a spread of various flavors of pulp adventure---vikingesque or sword-and-snowshoe (yes that is now a genre) in the North, jungles and lost temples out East, a whole mess of places for diplomacy or conquest or kingdom-building in the Scavenger Lands, sword-and-sandal in the treasure-hiding deserts down South, all sorts of nautical nonsense West, and courtly intrigue on the Blessed Isle. It's a lot more flexible than that, of course, but it lays out those various welcome mats and lets the players and ST come at them.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the world, I like how it outright reflects various real-world cultures and regions. This flings open the door for people to draw on real-life places, cultures, and myths they want to involve and lets players foster representation not just in physical features and dress but in culture, environment, etc.<br /> <br /> I agree with the Wizard up there particularly on point #2. The fact that Exalted lets you take concepts well beyond variations of warrior and crank them up to mythic levels is one of its biggest draws for me. The fact that I could very feasibly make a character who's a master of crochet <i>and have that be a viable way to contribute to the story</i> is something you don't see in a lot of games. Having a party where GLORIOUS SLIP-STITCH PRINCESS and METICULOUS ACCOUNTANT PRINCESS stand equal to INVINCIBLE SWORD PRINCESS and INESCAPABLE NINJA PRINCESS is cool as hell, and it's thanks to the game giving a lot of different things space and weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T12:18:05-08:00","id":1358916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1358892#post1358892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) You can have a concept like bureaucrat, blacksmith, socialite, preacher, sailor, etc, and the game actually supports making it a major part of your character, rather than an add-on to your combat focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a big one for me. I love the diversity of powers in the game supports a wide variety of functional and impactful characters, and helps avoid everything devolving into a &quot;when all you have is a hammer, all your problems are nails&quot; scenario with combat too often. That still happens a bit, but at least there's good mechanic support to attempt alternate resolutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T12:30:50-08:00","id":1358917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only#post1358884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me: I still love writing Charms (and I hope people enjoy what I recently wrote for <i>Exigents</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like what you wrote for Exigents.<br /> <br /> The thing I love the most about Exalted is that it changed my life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T12:45:41-08:00","id":1358918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1358916#post1358916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a big one for me. I love the diversity of powers in the game supports a wide variety of functional and impactful characters, and helps avoid everything devolving into a &amp;quot;when all you have is a hammer, all your problems are nails&amp;quot; scenario with combat too often. That still happens a bit, but at least there's good mechanic support to attempt alternate resolutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I should have put this at no.1, as it's the biggest one for me, and ultimately why I'm running Exalted rather than a different game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T13:15:57-08:00","id":1358922,"title":"","content":"The social system passes all but one of my &quot;Does this social system actually function?&quot; tests, which no other game I've seen can do without being an ultralight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T13:40:54-08:00","id":1358924,"title":"","content":"Won't post until I'm 100%.<br /> <br /> But thank you for this.<br /> <br /> Had been gearing myself up to stating that I needed a break for finding the direction of the forum the last few days very disillusioning. Every time I did, prayed for a thread like this.<br /> <br /> Not surprised it's from you.<br /> <br /> Back to bed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T13:52:40-08:00","id":1358926,"title":"","content":"Even if they don't get the same attention mechanically as combat, because that's always a bugbear, Exalted allows for characters to focus on a variety of archetypes and roles that have nothing to do with it, and supports doing legendary, memorable, magical stuff with those. The social system in 3e is fairly fleshed out and very evocative of how <i>people actually act</i>, which makes it feel both comprehensible and robust. It's a game that approaches its setting with an eye not for &quot;realism&quot; but <i>authenticity</i> in writing geopolitics, economy and cultural variety, and how mythic heroes and magic affect a world that bears these concerns, and asks you to explore the consequences of your actions. It draws from aesthetics and inspirations more numerous and expansive than a pastiche of &quot;medieval&quot; and pre-modern European fantasy. And charms can be quite a lot of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T14:09:48-08:00","id":1358928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1358924#post1358924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But thank you for this.<br /> <br /> Had been gearing myself up to stating that I needed a break for finding the direction of the forum the last few days very disillusioning. Every time I did, prayed for a thread like this.<br /> <br /> Not surprised it's from you.</div> </div> </div> </div>What high praise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1358922#post1358922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The social system passes all but one of my &quot;Does this social system actually function?&quot; tests, which no other game I've seen can do without being an ultralight.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are these tests, if I may ask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T14:10:20-08:00","id":1358929,"title":"","content":"I like that my character is not constrained by a class as in other games. You can have a religious bandit who uses a musical martial art, without having to worry if he/she is majorly a bard, a rogue, a monk or a cleric, and/or in what order you are gonna grow those sets of skills from level x to x+n.<br /> <br /> I love all the non-european fantasy elements. Also, the idea of esoteric martial arts is one of my favorite aspects of the setting/game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T14:45:01-08:00","id":1358935,"title":"","content":"I love the absurd stories we get to tell.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love the things I've had to look up.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love that this game got me into Howard and Zelazny and Martin and Tanith Lee.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love that the game has a group of crazed titans, desperately throwing themselves against the bars of their prison-bodies; that the game has a group of dead titans, psychically clawing at the worlds of the living and dead in a fit of nihilistic rage; but that the game can focus in on a trade dispute between two city-states, the intrigue surrounding a succession crisis, or a guy wandering from city to city and wrestling their strongest guys for money.<br /> <br /> I love that choke-slamming a city-god is perfectly acceptable first session behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T15:04:31-08:00","id":1358941,"title":"","content":"I love the way you have both a core of both a fairly sophisticated grounded understanding of historical politics and moral questions and ambiguous character and life as it was lived, that aren't out of place in literary period epics and drama, with absolute action+fantasy anime+CRPG nonsense! Really leaning hard into that kind of world and those kind of possibilities for character and story (and how RPGs are really well placed to play) is still an almost totally unique thing at close to the 20 year anniversary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T17:24:20-08:00","id":1358964,"title":"","content":"What I love best is that there is no clear line between who is the Hero and who is the Villain for the most part. Yes there are many injustices in the setting (at least from our outside perspective), but the Dragon-Blood who is guarding a convoy of Tribute to the Realm is often just as much a hero as the Lunar bandit that tries to waylay him to return the tribute to those it was taken from... or as villainous as the Solar pirate who wants to steal that booty for his own benefit.<br /> <br /> Everyone is the hero of their own stories... and while you may see yourself as a hero (and may even be hailed as such by some), others may see you as the villain... and both views are correct. There isn't a single Exalt type that can only be a hero or a villain... though some (Abyssals and Infernals) have an easier time being the bad guys than being the good guys. No one is &quot;pure&quot; good or &quot;pure&quot; evil... they just are who they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T17:55:11-08:00","id":1358968,"title":"","content":"People have said a lot of what I'd say already about the setting, mechanics, and so on. So, yeah, all that stuff.<br /> <br /> But... well... it's hard for me to not put a specific thing at number one:<br /> <br /> I met my wife when she saw the cover of Exalted 1e while I was reading it and she came over to talk to me... even if it wasn't the first RPG we ended up playing together... Harmonious Jade turned out to be a kick ass wing-woman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T18:29:46-08:00","id":1358971,"title":"","content":"Hmmm ok this is a lot to unpack (all good stuff though)<br /> <br /> For third edition, I love the system. I love the splats we have so far. I love that dragon bloods and lunars have given me an appreciation of where Solars fit. I love that even as a Dragon Blood one can feel like they are a powerful world shaking being. Their status shines, the way people treat them, the power isn't insignificant, and its just cool.<br /> <br /> I got to play a DB in an all solars game and at no point did I feel like the weak link. Even the solars were commenting on how much I contributed. It was fun.<br /> I love lunars now. They have a society that's well written and fun. Shape shifting is fun and trying to find ways to integrate it with the character is great. I like that lunars have many different ways to play now, not just Relentless Lunar Fury+ Deadly Beast man Transformation. <br /> <br /> The combat system is fun for me. The social system is great. It makes me want to play more characters with different knowledge of the world and everything.<br /> <br /> Can i just really summarize so I don't wind up rambling to just say I really like EX3? :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T18:35:55-08:00","id":1358972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1358928#post1358928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are these tests, if I may ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a simple set of common social tasks. I check if a social system:<br /> - Permits them to be attempted with reasonably well-defined mechanics<br /> - Has reasonably well-defined difficulties (that is, the GM doesn't have to invent a difficulty)<br /> - Does not leak important metainformation such as &quot;*dice clattter* Make a Detect Lies check. OK, your character thinks he's telling the truth even though you the player know you only make Detect Lies checks when you're lied to.&quot;<br /> <br /> The general list of tasks is:<br /> - The Basic Functions tests: Can you talk your way past a guard? Bribe an official to deal with your document first? Tearfully convince a detective that you really didn't do it? Con somebody into buying snake oil? Threaten a mob into standing down? Start a panic by yelling &quot;FIRE!&quot;? (Yes! 3E handles these basic use cases without issue.)<br /> - The Combat test: Assassin Alice attacks Diplomatic Dave. Can Dave talk down Alice during combat time? (Yes! 3E's social system functions just fine during combat.)<br /> - The Master Plan test: The king is dead, and Teenage Tim is the new king. Wicked Wally wants to be the power behind the throne. Can Wally gain young Tim's trust and get Tim to defer to him? And is this task appropriately difficult? (Yes and yes! Some intensive Instilling will get Wally where he wants to be, but it'll be a lot of work. Tim will know Wally's trying to curry favor and earn trust, but the mechanics don't tell Tim that Wally's rolling Manipulation.)<br /> - The Bidirectionality test: NPC Nancy wants to talk PC Paul into doing something, and she's pretty persuasive. Can Nancy try even if the GM couldn't talk his way out of a paper bag? (Yes! 3E's social system works on PCs too.)<br /> - The Evil Twin test: Heroic Harry and Allied Alan are waging war against Deceptive Dave, and Harry is waiting for Alan to tell him where to strike. Two messengers burst into the room. One says Alan's forces are fighting at Westville and need reinforcement immediately. The other says Alan's forces are fighting at Eastburg and need reinforcement immediately. Can Harry figure out which messenger is an imposter? (System failure, metainformation leak! Harry can only really interact with the situation through Read Intentions and Profile Character actions, both of which only give correct information or no information. Even if the fake's Guile beats Harry's RI or PC, Harry gets one count of &quot;Loyal to Alan, sir!&quot; or &quot;He's a messenger, he was out running through the woods until just recently&quot; and one count of &quot;403 ACCESS DENIED&quot; and the player immediately knows which is the fake despite failing the roll. Considering there's an entire splat of shapechanging tricksters, this is a pretty nasty oversight.)<br /> <br /> Beyond metainformation in the Evil Twin test there's a bit of a wart in that the system doesn't have any brakes that prevent &quot;Hi, nice to meet you, have an orange, let me give you a Defining tie of Loyalty towards me now&quot;. But it's the most functional system I've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T20:01:48-08:00","id":1358985,"title":"","content":"I love that the PCs in tonight\u2019s session <i>knew</i> Lionfolk were behind the recent attacks on villages, ran into some Lionfolk, and still stopped to say, \u201cWait, these might not be the right Lionfolk!\u201d<br /> <br /> I love that one of the PCs willingly gained a Derangement to feed the Fair Folk when she learned they were starving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-04-2020, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T21:04:47-08:00","id":1358993,"title":"","content":"I like three things mostly about Exalted.<br /> <br /> -Being the most glorious writer in the world is in fact a great avenue of power just like being the super swordsmen is and ninja of doom.<br /> <br /> -I love the fact that more then any other game I know, your character does have the power to change the world by sheer skill, smarts, luck, and power. You'll very very rarely be told that what you are doing is completely impossible for your character or that a goal is completely outside your reach. And if you do the game is very clear on what those things are in fact impossible.<br /> <br /> -And finally I because of the second point, I love that you can feel like a force of change for the better, At least to the best of your wisdom. Because it is not a question of power. This is more then anything why I love the Solar Exalted the most. They more then any other exalted fit such a narrative.<br /> <br /> That is not to say that no other exalted can do such as well, I just feel Solars fit the best to such a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T22:55:05-08:00","id":1359008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1358971#post1358971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can i just really summarize so I don't wind up rambling to just say I really like EX3? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>You certainly can. You can also ramble if you like! This is a positivity thread. Gushing is encouraged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T00:45:02-08:00","id":1359028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only#post1358884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As one of the freelance writers these days, I don't get too directly involved with the fan community, but Exalted has given me a lot of enjoyment and inspiration. I've seen &quot;positive responses only&quot; threads on other forums, and I think it'd be an interesting experiment for this one. Please join me in this experiment. I doubt we'll do it perfectly, but a good-faith effort would be appreciated. If it's been done already, well, the search function didn't reveal that to me, and also, who cares.<br /> <br /> For me: I still love writing Charms (and I hope people enjoy what I recently wrote for <i>Exigents</i>). I love the mythic weight of the Exalted. As someone who started with D&amp;D, I loved Exalted's willingness to address sex and sexuality, and love that we've been moving toward healthier ways to discuss those topics in the current edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The experience of performing epic feats using starting characters. The Brawl supernal is a very good substitute for going all Karna versus Arjuna. Someone in another thread listed some very good examples in the charms Nine Aeons Thew and Heaven Thunder Hammer, to which I'd also add Thunderclap Rush Attack/Thunderbolt Attack Prana, Dragon Coil Technique/Titan-Straightening Method and Crashing Wave Throw although I'm not quite certain if those let you bullrush someone and toss them into Extreme range. <br /> <br /> On that subject, the utilisation of abilities which aren't traditionally seen as heroic to perform heroic deeds. Fate-Shifting Solar Arete from Larceny comes to mind, although the once a day use is a bit of a shame. Emerald Induction Technique from Occult is also a great way to support a non-conventionally combat capable &quot;caster&quot; type character with a powerful and valuable being. The use of the Supernal mechanic to get these high level abilities at chargen is what really helps sell the premise, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T01:53:24-08:00","id":1359036,"title":"","content":"I'll restate what others have said and say that I like that there's so many different ways to be a hero and not just a warrior.<br /> <br /> I also like that you can be really powerful but still actually have to care about stuff, although that's more Ex3 than I felt in previous editions. There's some game systems out there that let you destroy cities, and lots of systems that make you have to care about the politics of the local imperial forces, but there's not quite so many that do both. I like a lot of the mystical philosophy elements of it as well, like the function of the gods, the Immaculate understanding of the elements, the dead's relationship with the living.<br /> <br /> There's a bunch of cool stuff that I can't really go too far in without making like a ten paragraph post though, like how cool and weighty sorcery is, cool locations in every single direction, how the Realm book made me think that an epic game about the Imperial Post service was 100% possible. Prior to that I was thinking like, walking around delivering love letters on a lazy afternoon, now I'm thinking like, hooves pounding on stone as an Exalted messenger drives their horse over a storm-wracked mountain to deliver a priority request for military aid while fending off the angry dead spirits of the mountain pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T06:25:15-08:00","id":1359057,"title":"","content":"I love Artifacts and Evocations. I love the <i>personality</i> in artifice.<br /> <br /> I love that I was able to simply describe<i> that a fight occurred in the past </i>between a Solar brawler with red jade gauntlets and a Lion Folk, describe a scorched chasm torn into the earth, and I could <i>see</i> the spark in the players\u2019 imaginations blaze to life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-05-2020, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T11:13:30-08:00","id":1359100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1358985#post1358985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love that the PCs in tonight\u2019s session <i>knew</i> Lionfolk were behind the recent attacks on villages, ran into some Lionfolk, and still stopped to say, \u201cWait, these might not be the right Lionfolk!\u201d<br /> <br /> I love that one of the PCs willingly gained a Derangement to feed the Fair Folk when she learned they were starving.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's great to see player investment/engagement like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T12:15:43-08:00","id":1359104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1358993#post1358993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Being the most glorious writer in the world is in fact a great avenue of power just like being the super swordsmen is and ninja of doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once had an Eclipse conqueror whose armies were equipped only with banners that read &quot;Surrender&quot; and &quot;Join Us.&quot; I love that the system lets that be viable.<br /> <br /> He also had a monstrous Full Moon mate for back-up, just in case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T12:41:49-08:00","id":1359108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1359104#post1359104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once had an Eclipse conqueror whose armies were equipped only with banners that read &quot;Surrender&quot; and &quot;Join Us.&quot; I love that the system lets that be viable.<br /> <br /> He also had a monstrous Full Moon mate for back-up, just in case.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;_&lt;... &gt;_&gt;... *Notes that for later use.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T12:45:43-08:00","id":1359109,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I would keep buying new Exalted books just to read all the elaborate, flowery Charm names.<br /> <br /> The actual game is fun too, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T15:00:48-08:00","id":1359151,"title":"","content":"First of all, I'd like to thank you for the thread. Discussions in the Internet naturally tend to focus on what we don't like, so such an &quot;[Exalted +]&quot; thread really helps you to recall that you actually like most things about the system you are playing.<br /> <br /> Things I love specifically about the Third Edition (in no particular order):<br /> <br /> - sorcerous workings,<br /> - martial arts, mastery and terrestrial tags, and overall writing of charms. It really <i>feels</i> like esoteric martial arts,<br /> - that the world is so open and full of mystery. Especially things like Yatani's children world, gate to Zen-Mu or &quot;yet stranger places for which second age has no name&quot;,<br /> - the Dreaming Sea,<br /> - gambits as a mechanics concept,<br /> - Dragon-Blooded, their charms and Immaculate martial arts. I really, really want to run them. Now they feel so cool that immediately upon meeting their first air immaculate and seeing what he can do, my Eclipse player asked: &quot;can I learn it?&quot;,<br /> - getimians,<br /> - exingents.<br /> <br /> Things about all three editions/ things which are specific to previous editions (in no particular order):<br /> <br /> - Well of Udr and Dowager's plan to escape Oblivion,<br /> - how open character creation is and how it allows you to focus on things other than combat,<br /> - generally, how many different tropes and motifs the setting accommodates: sword and sorcery, and dinosaurs!, and magitech warstriders!, and power armors!, and elemental kungf-fu masters! and kung-fu masters with weird fate manipulation! and five-mile long dragons. You really can have it all,<br /> - how shamelessly powerful players characters can be, things blowing up after you them with your arrows, casually walking through the doors, stealing things from behind glass in such a way that you forget you even owned them,<br /> - magitech,<br /> - Yu-Shan as a huge continent-city from Final Fantasy,<br /> - loom of fate as an actual object,<br /> - Sidereals, weird kung-fu fate secret agents who run the world,<br /> - Infernals and their cosmic progression,<br /> - Alchemicals!!!<br /> - weird, powerful, and large-scale magic,<br /> - how many weird corners there are to the setting: Faraway, Zen-Mu, Shining Answer, Sea of Mind, Oramus, and this strange world incinerated by Daystar,<br /> - how authors generally consistently have been trying to make sense of things and actually thing through how things should work in a world full of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 01-05-2020, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T01:46:59-08:00","id":1359224,"title":"","content":"Never had such intense drama in games, and I believe this is thanks to a very good social system. (Even though sometimes I have trouble managing it)<br /> <br /> I also love how the Great Curse is designed and how it allows for intense character progression or character reversal while still being fun for the player and the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T06:31:43-08:00","id":1359266,"title":"","content":"Perfect balance of Nuance &amp; Flavor vs Mundane &amp; Epic.<br /> <br /> The world is rich and varied but every player I ever had was hooked from the beginning and easily immersed. From the epic mythology to the day-to-day problem of back-end islanders.<br /> <br /> While combat is a big part of the system most of the abilities are not combat-related, which means the characters the PC comes up with are always interesting in other ways than their fancy fighting style. And in game they try far more often to avoid combat, just to try the other options. It's engaging and fuel their creativity. And yes you can be a monster in combat AND travel the world in order to become the best cook ever. Or jeweler. Or painter. Or just to meet people and make them laugh, one by one. And you can be a non-combatant and still be relevant to the story, which few games glimpse at.<br /> <br /> And when it's easy to do so for the PC it's also easy to flush your NPC just by looking at a the abilities and go &quot;yeah this one is a farmer but she has a passion for bird-watching and town-fairs with big-ass fires and dancing around them, sometimes in feathery robes&quot;.<br /> <br /> The character creation system is I find well balanced for all the things there is. And you never find yourself being discriminated against for having an &quot;interesting&quot; idea, on the contrary you find that you can ! Even in combat I haven't really seen a &quot;better&quot; style, but things more adapted to such and such situation. Which means as a Storyteller you can balance easy and hard encounters not as stats but as styles of ennemies and grow in your mastery of tension in fight at the same pace that your players gain confidence in their abilities.<br /> <br /> Narrative and cool is ENCOURAGED by the rules. Which is awesome. Really. I had players who have crazy ideas or take insane risks because the rules are not Constraints but Opportunities. THEY TRY THINGS. And that means all scenes can be source of great stories. (Also the 3rd Ed combat system is everything I never knew I ever wanted, especially the light/medium/heavy weapon with tags where &quot;you won't be penalized for wanting a scimitar&quot;.)<br /> <br /> Works on big and small scale. And by that I mean I ran a game in a custom setting where everyone is mortal (not even heroic at first !) and the combat system hold up perfectly ! Had 3 near TPK (they have the worst plans ever, I swear), if 2 or 3 rolls had gone differently and my players were high all the time on the epic-ness of everything even with mundane stats.<br /> <br /> The players can really chose how they characters will grow and change path if they want without being setback in reference of other characters.<br /> <br /> If someone wants to be a master of something, she can and she is. Now all the tension is on how will she use it. I love it.<br /> <br /> And all of this is even better because the way the book is written is truly Epic. Well done.<br /> <br /> I love this game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25608,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25608-crop-weaver","user":"Crop Weaver","date":". 01-06-2020, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25608-crop-weaver","name":"Crop Weaver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T06:44:48-08:00","id":1359270,"title":"","content":"Only downside : yes, there is homework for the Players too.<br /> <br /> You can't just show-up and expect that we will stop every time you have to roll because you don't know how this or that works. Well I was a Player (2ed) before Storyteller and it was fun to learn everything but not for everyone. Especially now that I have not English-speaking players.... But this is a Campaign system, so it is expected you put a little effort in this too. It's worth it, and your ST should have time for you and the other players too, between games. <br /> <br /> Only advice I have : if all but 1 or 2 at the table are new to this, go incremental. No grapple no sorcery no martial arts at the beginning. Learn 8 charms if 15 is too much at first, you won't have use for 15 of them in the first, or even first 2 games. Have simple stories too, since learning how this works will take a few tries. Even play mortals at first for a one-shot or two, as an intro !<br /> <br /> Look even in the downside part I am excited by the opportunities to play more xD<br /> <br /> Go try it, ask questions, make it yours.<br /> <br /> Exalt your game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25608-crop-weaver","name":"Crop Weaver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T07:33:35-08:00","id":1359284,"title":"","content":"I love the way that in Exalted you can go from roleplaying a character whose family treated them as a literal tool almost from birth and only taught them a dead language useful for magic, to running with your screaming ghost familiars and your found family through the streets of a burning, under-Chiaroscuro smuggler camp that you're jointly responsible for setting on fire in pursuit of the death cultists who honestly have a way lower bodycount in this city than your band of amoral showboats but are guilty of the crime of doing that &quot;horror movie monster gets up with an axe in its head when you turn your back&quot; thing.<br /> While not even sharing a language with a single member of your party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T15:21:25-08:00","id":1359360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1359284#post1359284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While not even sharing a language with a single member of your party.</div> </div> </div> </div>Step 1 in all of my games after character creation: &quot;Everyone gets a free language&quot; so we can avoid situations like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T16:12:26-08:00","id":1359369,"title":"","content":"I love how &quot;big&quot; sorcery is. In Dungeons and Dragons spells are basically bullets that you use and lose and need a night of rest to do again.... for some reason. Shadowrun has a good mechanic of Force vs Drain that fits that system... but Exalted. Oh Exalted. <br /> <br /> You can <i>start</i> with a spell the flays an enemy army. You can make yourself almost invulnerable with metal skin. You can fly on a tornado at 100 mph. You can call a storm from a clear day and sail on the sky with a boat you made from a peach. Its so wonderful and <b><i>Magical</i></b>. it feels like being a powerful sorcerer, and that's just rank 1! I also love mechanically how you never &quot;run out&quot; of Sorcery, its something you channel and will into being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T17:30:08-08:00","id":1359381,"title":"","content":"I love that I entered a group with the intent of making an Expy of Batman and <i>wasn't</i> the most outlandish PC concept in the group.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love that I entered a group with the intent of making an Expy of Batman, and instead of saying no, the ST said, &quot;It's gonna be interesting to see you interact with the two assassins in the party.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bI love that I create a character that's fantastically wealthy and that doesn't even especially take that many character points to make happen.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love that when creating a character that's fantastically wealthy, the game doesn't let me get away without a reminder that such a pile of money is tied to large-scale human suffering.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love that if your fantastically-wealthy character has a problem with the blood on his money, he can <i>try to fix that</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T19:39:41-08:00","id":1359394,"title":"","content":"The setting is awesome! The Storyteller system is flexible.<br /> <br /> The general freedom this game gives to carve out into our own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8757-pram","name":"Pram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T08:58:08-08:00","id":1359502,"title":"","content":"I'm very fond of Exaltation itself as a way of communicating who has power in the setting. Your typical level 1 D&amp;D adventure party might be treated as armed vagabonds, glorified exterminators, trophy hunting tourists, to fantasy super heroes depending on your setting/edition/DM.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T11:16:45-08:00","id":1359529,"title":"","content":"I really enjoy how making characters seem to enrich the setting, as opposed to taking away from it. Imagining characters into existence seem to broaden as opposed to exhaust the horizons of the setting, in terms of the implications they have on life in the world of Exalted, what in-setting variety the richness of concepts are drawn from and so on. I suppose it's a matter of utilizing system constraints in a generative manner rather than in a limiting way. Not sure if this comes up in design conversations, but I figure it's an overall strength of where things are in Exalted now. It's possible that it always has been and I'm only noticing it now given I haven't always had the chance to play in the almost 2 decades I've been following the game line. Nevertheless, it seemed worth mentioning in light of the upcoming Exigents book.<br /> <br /> <br /> For I have always loved the animism of the world of Exalted which has so many different perspectives on seemingly the same thing that may nonetheless open to divergent realities. This is a setting where thousands deities and more walk the world with casually different modes of being and views on the world. I imagine this will play out in its own scale in the Exigents. The premise of Exigents has been the thing that excited me the most lately in this game. Just thinking about the variety of character concepts one can generate out of it and how much each individual Exigent can potentially add to the breadth and scope of the world is something I'm really looking forward. And if it also has some level of conceptual manipulation as a way Charms interact with the world then I'm pretty much set for life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":81,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/81-vx3","user":"VX3","date":". 01-07-2020, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/81-vx3","name":"VX3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar81_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T16:27:59-08:00","id":1359601,"title":"","content":"I remember starting to read my first Exalted books in 2003. I was a big anime <br /> fan, and having an anime inspired RPG by White Wolf was a big draw. I was a big Vampire &amp; Mage fan back <br /> then, and found the &quot;before the world of darkness&quot; <br /> speel rather evocative. (I know that idea got abandoned long ago.) <br /> The idea of being a &quot;powerful&quot; PC with more agency right out of the gate was a breath of fresh air.<br /> <br /> I ran with the game as a sandbox with character driven story and had an amazing time. I've never had more fun than playing Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T06:30:38-08:00","id":1359704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1359381#post1359381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love that I entered a group with the intent of making an Expy of Batman and <i>wasn't</i> the most outlandish PC concept in the group.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love that I entered a group with the intent of making an Expy of Batman, and instead of saying no, the ST said, &quot;It's gonna be interesting to see you interact with the two assassins in the party.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bI love that I create a character that's fantastically wealthy and that doesn't even especially take that many character points to make happen.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love that when creating a character that's fantastically wealthy, the game doesn't let me get away without a reminder that such a pile of money is tied to large-scale human suffering.<br /> <br /> \u200bI love that if your fantastically-wealthy character has a problem with the blood on his money, he can <i>try to fix that</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that you mention it, I had a lot of (slightly traumatic) fun with my &quot;what if Dave Strider were Batman&quot; Night Caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T07:27:16-08:00","id":1359720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1359704#post1359704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that you mention it, I had a lot of (slightly traumatic) fun with my &quot;what if Dave Strider were Batman&quot; Night Caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind doing a storytime, sometime? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd love to compare notes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T07:40:18-08:00","id":1359724,"title":"","content":"I just love the Exalted setting so much. It sparks my imagination like no other fictional world, and keeps me coming back despite my horrible track record with using Exalted mechanics.<br /> <br /> I love the 3e social influence system. I've never seen another social system that's so easy to grasp, yet consistently produces results that feel intuitive and realistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T19:39:52-08:00","id":1359830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1359720#post1359720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind doing a storytime, sometime? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd love to compare notes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! In the interest of sparing uninterested parties a wall of text, I'll write it in spoiler brackets.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Daven Sadara was a Chiaroscuro native of the &quot;street rat with obvious foreign ancestry&quot; variety. He was the leader of a small gang, a self-appointed neighborhood watch. In his free time, he liked poetry and other performing arts. He Exalted when he got in over his head with a criminal syndicate, then felt a pull to a First Age tomb where he got a) a Circle, and b) a sweet artifact reaper daiklave and cowl. He became known as the Ghost in the Glass, a local vigilante, but it became harder and harder to separate his Solar secret identity (the &quot;Knight,&quot; based on his iconic anima) from his other secret identity--one was a local symbol of hope, and the other was an Anathema that would bring misfortune down upon everyone. He decided to give the cowl to his intense outcaste brother... but said bro started going too far, perhaps challenging the Knight to stop him.<br /> <br /> Daven was a little too genre-savvy for his own good--his awareness that as a Solar he was <i>more</i> than almost everyone else was isolating and filled him with indecision. He was extremely good at finding flaws in others' plans, but this put him at odds with a prideful former-Dynast Circlemate (not coincidentally, as the other player and I were falling out of friendship). Things were heading to a low point, but time constraints and the divided gaming group got in the way of the campaign. We hope to restart it someday.<br /> <br /> Other miscellaneous events that occurred: collecting Lunars; multiple &quot;he dropped his smoked glasses, he's serious&quot; moments; rooftop sex with a dangerous Abyssal; rescuing his long-lost sister from a Delzahn-run brothel; kicking Fair Folk ass in &quot;flashball,&quot; a cross between soccer and blitzball; and debating justice with a shikari when he could've just killed her instead.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 01-08-2020, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T20:01:00-08:00","id":1359832,"title":"","content":"I love the feeling of low-key anxiety transfiguring into intense satisfaction when the ST awards your description a three-point stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T10:53:25-08:00","id":1359922,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of magic as sufficiently advanced skill. Each Ability giving access to some awesome tricks lets a wide variety of character concepts not only be effective but also feel cool to play. In-setting, it also really supports the idea of Essence being the building blocks of Creation, in that magic seems to be in everything. I'd say that this is probably the one most fundamental design choice that makes Exalted feel like Exalted for me.<br /> <br /> I love how thematically strong the main Hosts of Exaltations are. It restricts you in just the right way to make you creative. Some power sets in Exalted that I read years ago still pop up in my head and make me giggle with delight.<span style=\"font-size:9px\"> Throne Shadow Style.</span><br /> <br /> And, honestly, I love perfect effects. I know they're bad for many reasons, but I came in during the middle of 2e, and Seven Shadows Evasion for 3m at Essence 2 made a statement about the game that I'm 100% sure is part of what drew me in. 3e is surely a much more playable, healthy game, but god damn, I can not get over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T19:40:41-08:00","id":1360031,"title":"","content":"I love Weimann's signature. It's really understated, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T01:17:32-08:00","id":1360082,"title":"","content":"The power scale doesn't affect the ability to have great games and amazing stories.<br /> <br /> When I asked my 1st ST how 'strong' a Solar could be he answered with &quot;we have the stats for mountains as improvised weapons. And the ways for you to dodge it&quot;. I was hooked","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25608-crop-weaver","name":"Crop Weaver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T10:15:31-08:00","id":1360152,"title":"","content":"DEEEEEEEEELETED.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 01-10-2020, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T07:54:01-08:00","id":1360318,"title":"","content":"There are few things about Exalted that I don't love.<br /> <br /> I love the way the universe is crafted using myths as inspiration to tell stories about the dangers of empire and great men, and the flaws in heroes, and the idea that there is a whole broken world out there but godamn it, you have agency if nothing else, and ways to change the setting and learn to live with those changes along the way.<br /> <br /> Along the way, I shared in inspired, epic stories with friends both online and offline using this universe as an always renewed jumping board, and the reflexions about these stories made me want to learn how to tell them better. And here is where the beauty of Exalted lies for me : in order to craft better stories, it gets you to read about our world's history, it points you towards anthropology and sociology and political issues that *matter*, here in our world. It's a great tool, a great prism to understand and learn. And along the way, you can be tossed through a palace wall as a living bronze statue to save a ruler from demon assassins in order to use him as a political puppet later (and if this sounds specific, it's because it is.)<br /> <br /> I love Exalted. I love this bizarre cocktail of fantasy and realpolitik that can simmer for years to grant iconic moments of awesome.<br /> <br /> And the maps are nice, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","user":"LeTipex","date":". 01-11-2020, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T12:35:03-08:00","id":1360366,"title":"","content":"The options it gives the players.<br /> I'm not too familiar with many RPGs but I like the customization the system allows.<br /> Evocations and charms are a neat way to build characters with some decent room for interpretation. <br /> <br /> I also like the cosmology and mythos that was built up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T07:58:00-08:00","id":1360880,"title":"","content":"It's been about a week, and this experiment got to 4 pages. Along the way it made multiple people's day a little better. It certainly did for me.<br /> <br /> Thank you all for participating, and thank you also for sticking with the thread's premise. Perhaps we can have more [Positive] or [+] threads in the future. They don't spawn dozen-page arguments, but I personally think quality of time spent on this forum trumps amount of time. And several people are clearly hungry for more positivity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T03:30:49-08:00","id":1361045,"title":"","content":"I think we're also pretty good when we're talking about our own characters and games. A discussion about games set in the Dreams of the First Age setting would probably go very differently to a discussion of the overall value of the supplement.<br /> <br /> I personally, feel that we perhaps have too many megathreads where interesting ideas sometimes get shared in a very driveby fashion that doesn't invite much in the way of response before the topic has lurched forward to its next destination. There's still a use to those threads but sometimes I come online and see the same few topics bumped in a slightly different order and people's ideas deserve better than that imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-15-2020, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T04:29:46-08:00","id":1361051,"title":"","content":"I must admit I'm some sort of an abuser of &quot;Ask a question, get an answer&quot; because well ... I have a lot of questions, on many different topics. Maybe opening some sort of subtopics for questions and answers or something like that ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T06:42:40-08:00","id":1361066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1361051#post1361051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must admit I'm some sort of an abuser of &quot;Ask a question, get an answer&quot; because well ... I have a lot of questions, on many different topics. Maybe opening some sort of subtopics for questions and answers or something like that ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember people used to just make new threads titled with the question they were after. Don't see any reason why you can't do that? Alternatively you could try to put several questions under one broad topic, if that's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T08:54:13-08:00","id":1361284,"title":"","content":"I love Exalted for many reasons, but oddly a lot of them are the opposite of why I love the oWoD.<br /> <br /> 1.) I love we can make The Big Damn Hero(ine)s.<br /> <br /> They can cure cancer.<br /> They can save the world.<br /> Then save it again, 'cause some new threat is trying to fill the power-vacuum of the old threat.<br /> Then decide it's time to nip this power-vacuum none-sense in the bud &amp; SAVE THE WORLD FOREVER.<br /> <br /> I love that the PCs' ability to be awesome is limited only by our imagination, ambition, &amp; how pumped we can get the ST into the gonzo ideas spawning in our heads.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T14:22:43-08:00","id":1362731,"title":"","content":"Why do I love Exalted, you ask?<br /> <br /> Because it allowed me to play a game where Snidley Whiplash, The Rock, and Domon Kasshu all get into a mecha wrestling match with Dracula.<br /> <br /> Because it allowed me to brag that I had a game where I became a relationship counselor to a T-Rex as a plot point.<br /> <br /> Because it made me realize as a GM, the power of just letting my players have fun in a sandbox before they inevitably set it on fire<br /> <br /> And because it made me realize there's more than just DnD out there, so it really broadened my horizons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T00:18:14-08:00","id":1362810,"title":"","content":"This could be an edit to my previous post, but then it would get unnoticed and I treat it as my public &quot;thank you&quot; to the developers. I love:<br /> <br /> - Forest Witches and the Sea of Mind;<br /> - Yatani's children;<br /> - &quot;[M]onstrous forces assailed Creation, threatening to crush the world. Some came from the chaos beyond reality\u2019s edge, others from dark and vasty depths under the world, and <i>yet more from places that the Second Age has no name for or language to describe</i>.&quot; (AoTC, pp.147-148).<br /> <br /> Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 01-23-2020, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T16:04:33-08:00","id":1365386,"title":"","content":"Okay, focus on the positive, focus on the positive, been drifting too much...<br /> <br /> A thing I felt an attachment to very early on in Exalted was the presentation of Charms. I like that notion of magic and character powers primarily provided in the form of things that grew out of and focused skills and similar qualities. It keeps there from being an awkward dichotomy between the superpowered and the mundane and provides clear focus on what the practical applications of all of these powers are, especially useful for all of the things that aren't merely combative. Even back then, they felt very rich with personality.<br /> <br /> I like the Caste names and marks (and the Aspects and associated symbols), for how striking and direct and iconic they are.<br /> <br /> I always liked the name &quot;Realm Defence Grid&quot; in combination with descriptions of the kinds of munitions that were actually directed at the Fair Folk. I don't know what it was, but something about it really quickly hit me with the dividing line between the ancient world looking setting and the super powerful high tech (but still pulpy looking) weapon commanded by its most powerful ruler. It just kind of shot me with an infusion of what the core appeal of the setting was.<br /> <br /> Gosh darn do I miss that wiki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T20:31:17-08:00","id":1365454,"title":"","content":"I love that there is a system which makes Dueling possible. A lot of games make combat a pretty static Hit vs Defense and there's no way to be creative or cool with trading blows outside of narration. <br /> <br /> In Exalted though, gaddamn. There're animal styles, weapon specific styles, an anti army style, and a bunch of not-fighting-but-actually fighting styles. And the regular charms of Melee, Brawl, Archery, and Thrown. And you can mic and match! They also combo with support abilities- Dodge, Resistance, Stealth and Athletics. <br /> <br /> The iaijutsu ronin, a wrestler, a boxer, a singer, an assassin, and a hatchet thrower are all completely unique fighters mechanically and I love that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T20:51:56-08:00","id":1365466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1365454#post1365454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love that there is a system which makes Dueling possible. A lot of games make combat a pretty static Hit vs Defense and there's no way to be creative or cool with trading blows outside of narration.<br /> <br /> In Exalted though, gaddamn. There're animal styles, weapon specific styles, an anti army style, and a bunch of not-fighting-but-actually fighting styles. And the regular charms of Melee, Brawl, Archery, and Thrown. And you can mic and match! They also combo with support abilities- Dodge, Resistance, Stealth and Athletics.<br /> <br /> The iaijutsu ronin, a wrestler, a boxer, a singer, an assassin, and a hatchet thrower are all completely unique fighters mechanically and I love that</div> </div> </div> </div>Forget all of that, you can have interesting decisions in dueling <i>without</i> all this magic mumbo-jumbo. <br /> When to Decisive, tactical delaying to clash or double-attack, fishing for that 2-point Stunt bonus, you've got a basic combat system that does away with the need for dueling blenders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T21:54:02-08:00","id":1365476,"title":"","content":"Punching out a tyrant lizard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T14:42:26-08:00","id":1365614,"title":"","content":"<b>In general:</b><br /> - The setting is what drives me to ST Exalted since the First Edition. It's full of magic and exotism and speaks to the part of me that loved anthropology classes back in college.<br /> <b>3E:</b><br /> - The crafting system (unpopular opinion, I know)<br /> - The Lunars<br /> - The social system<br /> - Some other bits and pieces, but I'm trying to stay focused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>Inevitable Meerkat Style</b></i><br /> <i>The Student Sutra of Spotlight Hoging: Once, there was a maiden, but who cares about those? Let's talk about Lunars.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8863-slulura","name":"Slulura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T15:36:36-08:00","id":1365622,"title":"","content":"The Setting has been Exalted's strong point since day one.<br /> <br /> But with new 3rd ed the open fun sandboxiness of Sorcery and Artifacts are a major Draw.<br /> <br /> But I love the Metaphysics and how they combine with the Anthropology fanfiction of Creation.<br /> <br /> And the fact we have a solid method of defining social endeavors and projects (yes I too enjoy the crafting system) I am quite happy. In fact I usually have been hacking apart the Social system of 3rd ed and porting it into my World of Darkness games like Werewolf and Changeling. Its hard to go back once you've been introduced to the Intimacies system. Basically I just always add Integrity into the rule sets and I'm mostly good. It even fits better for certain rules in say Werewolf for instance for meditating to regain Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T03:19:21-07:00","id":1375919,"title":"","content":"I love the look of envy people give me when I tell them about my latest game session.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026and the last thing the necromancer saw before life fled her body was Lyse\u2019s form flowing and melting into her own.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDamn, your game sounds awesome.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T04:29:40-07:00","id":1375930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1365622#post1365622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the fact we have a solid method of defining social endeavors and projects (yes I too enjoy the crafting system) I am quite happy. In fact I usually have been hacking apart the Social system of 3rd ed and porting it into my World of Darkness games like Werewolf and Changeling. Its hard to go back once you've been introduced to the Intimacies system. Basically I just always add Integrity into the rule sets and I'm mostly good. It even fits better for certain rules in say Werewolf for instance for meditating to regain Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I relate to this so much. I had a few DD games since, and every social situation I've found myself in was more boring when game mechanics were called to deal with the situations, compared to Exalted they really lack of everything","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T05:19:47-07:00","id":1375935,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve mentioned it before, but it really deserves its own post:<br /> <br /> Stunting. <br /> <br /> Many tabletop games I\u2019ve played give almost all the descriptive power to the person running the game, and leaves players <i>hoping</i> their action ends up being cool (and, at least in my experience as a player, quietly worrying that the GM will describe their action with something humiliating if they happen to roll a one). Exalted doesn\u2019t just give control of the visuals of the PCs\u2019 actions to the players - it tells them to <i>go wild</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-21-2020, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T05:28:32-07:00","id":1375938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1375935#post1375935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve mentioned it before, but it really deserves its own post:<br /> <br /> Stunting.<br /> <br /> Many tabletop games I\u2019ve played give almost all the descriptive power to the person running the game, and leaves players <i>hoping</i> their action ends up being cool (and, at least in my experience as a player, quietly worrying that the GM will describe their action with something humiliating if they happen to roll a one). Exalted doesn\u2019t just give control of the visuals of the PCs\u2019 actions to the players - it tells them to <i>go wild</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed Exalted taught me to do this even in games where I do not usually stunt. I just more naturally ask players : &quot;So how's your fireball, and describe the kind of explosion it makes ?&quot; and it all goes more naturally and the players of other games usually embrace it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T06:53:03-07:00","id":1375952,"title":"","content":"I liked how there's always things and superpowers for anything a human can do. <br /> <br /> There's always a question in any fantasy or superpowered setting. &quot;why is it that you rule? Just because you've got superpowers doesn't mean that you would be a good at leadership, or skilled at management, or being inspirational to your subordinates, all things which a leader needs.&quot; <br /> <br /> Well, in exalted, they can do all that. Their powers aren't just for fighting and punching and smashing shit or snapping out insane inventions. They're also for running an organisation smoothly, bringing people together, sending out oratory that can send entire nations to their knees, and producing beautiful works of art. It's truly a different thing from what I've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T07:32:00-07:00","id":1375961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1375952#post1375952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's always a question in any fantasy or superpowered setting. &quot;why is it that you rule? Just because you've got superpowers doesn't mean that you would be a good at leadership, or skilled at management, or being inspirational to your subordinates, all things which a leader needs.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, in exalted, they can do all that. Their powers aren't just for fighting and punching and smashing shit or snapping out insane inventions. They're also for running an organisation smoothly, bringing people together, sending out oratory that can send entire nations to their knees, and producing beautiful works of art. It's truly a different thing from what I've seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, you can still question <b>if </b>that truly makes you more fit to rule; after all, you could do all those things as a highly-placed civil servant.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, it's rather nice that the skills a leader has in Exalted are not necessarily tied to their effectiveness at swinging a sword or slinging fireballs (even if those <i>are</i> how they end up with a crown on their head).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T07:45:27-07:00","id":1375964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1375961#post1375961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to be fair, you can still question <b>if </b>that truly makes you more fit to rule; after all, you could do all those things as a highly-placed civil servant.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, it's rather nice that the skills a leader has in Exalted are not necessarily tied to their effectiveness at swinging a sword or slinging fireballs (even if those <i>are</i> how they end up with a crown on their head).</div> </div> </div> </div>well, to be pedantic, Solar powers work really really well when they're at the top of the organisation. Besides, your own powers grow to the point where it's not 'highly placed civil servant' but instead 'elder statesman who basically runs everything'. <br /> <br /> And another thing. You always see 'powerful but unskilled' shit in all kinds of media. Exalted are different. Your powers explode right from your skills. And it encompasses everything. You don't get mortals saying 'yeah, you can fire out blasts, but I'm better at you in [insert subject here]'. It isn't the cheap 'I'm superior because i can throw fireball'. It's something more than that. <br /> <br /> For some unknown reason, I find such an arrangement strangely compelling. I've seen lots of fictions where the supervillain claims that he's a superior species because he's got the power over magnetism and is objectively the best ruler. I've never really seen fictions where the supervillain claims that he's the superior being and is objectively the best ruler and has a chance that he is right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T08:10:04-07:00","id":1375969,"title":"","content":"I love that skills such as Linguistics are a thing and they seem to be just as powerful in their context as the combat skills are for their context. <br /> It's what made me fall in love with Exalted and my favorite character I played was a Linguistics supernal with a secondary focus on bureaucracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12021-scream","name":"Scream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T12:31:46-07:00","id":1375994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1375952#post1375952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked how there's always things and superpowers for anything a human can do.<br /> <br /> There's always a question in any fantasy or superpowered setting. &quot;why is it that you rule? Just because you've got superpowers doesn't mean that you would be a good at leadership, or skilled at management, or being inspirational to your subordinates, all things which a leader needs.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. I mean, I love that Exalted adds &quot;I am efficient bureaucrat to a supernatural degree&quot; to the palette of why supernatural rulers *are* supernatural rulers.<br /> <br /> I am less sure that they would always be who you exactly want *in charge* relative to some sorceress who can routinely pump out all manner of magical enhancements to her country. There are lots of benefits to having that person in charge, always making the last call, always in the room as the person to please when dealing with foreign governments, that you don't get just by putting them in a subordinate role and putting the supreme magical manager in the hot seat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T12:35:31-07:00","id":1375995,"title":"","content":"Romance between Solars and Lunars. Or Solars and Lunars who aren\u2019t romantically involved dealing with their mate having feelings for someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T08:11:43-07:00","id":1376113,"title":"","content":"I love the cycle of strife and redemption. A \u201cgood\u201d character can go too far in the pursuit of \u201cgood\u201d and lose their way, but the intervention of a pure-hearted individual or the love of something beyond themself can bring them back to who they meant to be.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a major theme for my current character, and it\u2019s an interesting part of my group. What is a \u2018hero\u2019 is a great thing to explore in Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T08:53:25-07:00","id":1376117,"title":"","content":"I love that the skills of the athlete and the warrior can be as magical as the skills of the scholar, and that the skills for applying medicine to heal people are central to the ability to heal people with magic, rather than redundant in the face of healing spells.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm upset that there are no spells that heal or help with healing.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm upset about the arbitrary lines drawn between &quot;combat skills&quot; and &quot;martial arts&quot;, when combat arts are martial skills and martial skills are combat arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T02:07:37-07:00","id":1376494,"title":"","content":"Oh golly, where do I start?<br /> <br /> How about the blistering gonzo high-flying giant-sword-slinging wuxia anime action set in a sword-and-sorcery weird fantasy setting that genuinely feels strange and unique?<br /> <br /> Or how every character concept has a bit of magic to them by nature of the charm-based system?<br /> <br /> Maybe it's the fact that the conceptual (and literal) color palette is so vibrant I can taste the rainbow whenever I think about the game?<br /> <br /> Could it be because it offers up an experience decidedly different from the Dungeons and Dragons norm that I grew up with?<br /> <br /> I'll tell you what, though - whenever I think I'm done with Exalted, if only for awhile, it doesn't go away. It waits, patiently, until the time is right. And then the interest comes roaring back, as strong as it ever was.<br /> <br /> Time has passed. I'm a changed man. So much of me, my life, my opinions, my beliefs, my situation is different now from when my love first blossomed... and some things just haven't changed at all. Exalted is still there. And I suspect it always will be.<br /> <br /> If anything wants to unseat Exalted in my heart, it's going to have a heck of a time doing so.<br /> <br /> I just wish they'd get those darn books out faster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T17:22:27-07:00","id":1377020,"title":"","content":"I love the setting of Exalted as a place that has a large and complex ecosystem/social structure of gods such that there are not only the likes of your local field god but they're people who can form an integral part of the community and engage in their own participation in politics and spirituality. Plus the distinctions of what Heaven and its residents mean in this layout, and the frosty relationships between these sides.<br /> <br /> I love it even more now that the potential for Exaltation is extended to those small gods, in addition to the obstacles and costs associated with that grace, and the reflections it might drive gods to take part in.<br /> <br /> Why, I don't believe I know of many other fantasy settings that include even the particulars there, let alone what emerges from the combined melange of it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T13:34:00-07:00","id":1377222,"title":"","content":"Going back to how &quot;everyone can be a wizard, even the warrior&quot;, there's also &quot;everyone can practice kung fu, not just the warriors&quot;.<br /> <br /> That is to say, traditional women who are stay-at-home mothers can be Exalted, and be just as powerful as traditional warrior men Exalted, in different fields.<br /> <br /> Crafting, Medicine, Lore, Integrity, Presence, Performance, Bureaucracy... You can spin the world on the new axis that is you without ever learning how to fight. While this is harder for Celestial Exalted in the Second Age, it's always been an option for Dragon-Blooded because the communities they can form through sheer numbers.<br /> <br /> <br /> In most kung fu anime and similar franchises, non-combat super-agency doesn't generally happen.<br /> <br /> In <i>Dragon Ball Z</i>, you generally need to be a Saiyan warrior or a genius inventor to mean anything.<br /> <br /> In <i>RWBY</i>, Aura is like <i>DBZ</i> Ki in that it's only really accessible (and useful) to warriors. The rules about Semblances are unclear in this regard, but it also seems that most Semblances do not appear until you undergo the training to become a warrior, which necessarily excludes traditional housewives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T19:04:02-07:00","id":1377256,"title":"","content":"Not to mention stay-at-home fathers and traditional warrior-women. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T21:21:38-07:00","id":1377276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1377256#post1377256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention stay-at-home fathers and traditional warrior-women. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this <i>is</i> a fantasy setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm not saying that women fighting or being warriors is fantastic, though it was historically rare. I was specifically referring to &quot;traditional warrior-women&quot; as an entire social caste, which is unheard of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-30-2020, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T23:25:26-07:00","id":1377297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1377276#post1377276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this <i>is</i> a fantasy setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's so fantastical about women fighting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T23:54:56-07:00","id":1377301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1377297#post1377297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's so fantastical about women fighting?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't usually see it well, normally. In the real world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T00:19:32-07:00","id":1377306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1377301#post1377301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't usually see it well, normally. In the real world</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people don't know to <i>look for it</i> in the real world. But evidence suggests that women have fought in virtually every war in history, even if they had to hide their genders to do it. Hell, Shaka Zulu had an entire force of exclusively-female fighters.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust because people like Mike Pence feel that women shouldn't fight in the military, doesn't mean they're not going to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T01:46:34-07:00","id":1377314,"title":"","content":"It's rarely been common, but it has certainly happened many times.<br /> <br /> Especially in sieges.<br /> <br /> (I also think &quot;traditional stay-at-home mothers&quot; is a bit anachronistic because peasants for most of history were way too poor for anyone to not work... but also work was done largely in/from the home anyway.)<br /> <br /> Actually, that's one thing I like about Exalted; by deliberately trying to big-up female and LGBT roles, it sometimes is actually more realistic than more &quot;historical&quot; settings. Not perfectly, because it's trying to be accessible rather than realistic. The presentation of LGBT people is more like modern views than the multiple, varied and complex (and often negative, but in a different way to modern homophobes) historical views of LGBT people, for example. <i>But </i>a lot of what people think is &quot;historical&quot; with regards to gender and societal roles is very much a simplification (and often based on projecting 17th century norms backwards into much less strict societies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-30-2020, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T06:33:38-07:00","id":1377333,"title":"","content":"Hmm... In the sense of literally staying at home*, well... Exalted Core is *kind* of unfriendly in its general 'tude to even scholars who want to stay in their library, compared to two-fisted action archaeologists and such. (Which I of course endorse as fully right and proper to portraying the right atmosphere of pulpy brio and &quot;Savage Adventure&quot;!). The old idea that in the world of Exalted, everyone should know some kung-fu etc.<br /> <br /> But in the sense of &quot;Broadly have the skills thought to be typical of&quot;, even if not literally staying at home. Yes, sure absolutely.<br /> <br /> (And it is pretty cool to have such extensions of many suites of skills! It is also an oft pitfall of Exalted that it means gesturing for powers that not always plentifully in genre media can lead to writers coming up with some odd and wonky stuff, but let's focus on the positive ITT!).<br /> <br /> * As is the current style of the times <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T08:27:56-07:00","id":1377348,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>I'm going to draw a line under discussing the roles of the sexes in regard to Creation/Exaltation because it's off-topic and has the potential to make the experience of this thread rather negative.<br /> <br /> It's a reasonable basis for discussion elsewhere but please, not here. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-30-2020, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T18:41:52-07:00","id":1377621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1377333#post1377333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense of literally staying at home... As is the current style of the times <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not me, I'm still going to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1377333#post1377333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">let's focus on the positive ITT!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, let's.<br /> <br /> I love the Intimacy system. It's so nice that what a character cares about can make it easier or harder, or even impossible, to persuade them to take certain actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-31-2020, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T18:53:05-07:00","id":1377624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1377621#post1377621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not me, I'm still going to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, my condolences.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love the Intimacy system. It's so nice that what a character cares about can make it easier or harder, or even impossible, to persuade them to take certain actions. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's great. A definite improvement on Second Edition's social traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T22:51:38-07:00","id":1380319,"title":"","content":"I love reading Charms and imagining how different characters might express them differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T22:53:39-07:00","id":1380320,"title":"","content":"I love the setting. I love it to bits. It's so in depth and it feels like a real place where real people live and act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T23:12:44-07:00","id":1380324,"title":"","content":"^ Seconding this. Lots of games have good settings. Exalted's is another level.<br /> <br /> The Directions, the Underworld, Malfeas... you can tell so many different style of stories and it still feels part of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-11-2020, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T08:36:02-07:00","id":1380656,"title":"","content":"I love writing Evocations, creating a legend with every item I introduce to the game. I love it all the more because I didn't expect to enjoy this facet of Ex3. &quot;How many damn powers do they expect me to write?!&quot;<br /> <br /> I love the fact that my friends still quote lines and talk about scenes from our first game (back in 1st &amp; 2nd Ed) 15+ years ago, and how such talk encouraged new players to brave the book and join into a new game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T06:55:51-07:00","id":1420814,"title":"","content":"I love that one of my new players for a Lunar game asked if it was okay for their character to have a gang of sea-slug folk to scavenge the cargoes out of sunken wrecks near Chiaroscuro, something I never would have even imagined, but now has to be in my game.<br /> <br /> For that matter, I friggin\u2019 love the new Lunars book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T19:00:24-07:00","id":1420917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Artful Maiming Onslaught</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scars left on players\u2019 characters look cool rather than disfiguring, unless the player desires otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2018Nuff said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T19:09:53-08:00","id":1421547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358884-what-do-you-love-about-exalted-positive-responses-only?p=1420917#post1420917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2018Nuff said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, I have a lunar character right now in a game who has massively disfiguring scars on his face, but only because I chose to have them inititally and chose to have them made worse by an injury in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26249-keelbreaker","name":"Keelbreaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T03:48:26-08:00","id":1421584,"title":"","content":"I really love the weird amount of artifacts and how interesting the different effects are. <br /> <br /> on an unrelated note, I love Sword and Sorcery and the Bronze Age setting. I don't know how much is really Bronze Age in practice, but its cool anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T04:01:58-08:00","id":1421587,"title":"","content":"How epic in scope it is<br /> <br /> Also the whole Solar-Lunar bond thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}